    "ExplanationWrongC": "A forward rate above the spot rate (F > S) indicates a forward PREMIUM — the currency is expected to STRENGTHEN (appreciate), not depreciate. When the yen costs more in the forward market ($0.00918 vs. $0.0091 spot), the market expects the yen to appreciate against the dollar. This interpretation follows from the numerator convention (F − S): a positive numerator signals that the market prices the currency to strengthen.",
