    "Stem": "Flash Tech is all-equity financed with an unlevered cost of equity of 12.0% and 100 million shares outstanding at $20 each. The CFO is considering recapitalizing by issuing $400 million of debt at a 6.0% pre-tax cost and using the proceeds to repurchase shares at $20. The marginal tax rate is 25%. Using MM Proposition II with taxes, what is the new cost of equity, and what is the new WACC?",
